  "description": "MORNING LANE",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The advertisement signage, by its inappropriate size, scale, and detailed design, would result in an overly dominant, discordant, and visually intrusive structure that fails to respect the character of the host building and fails to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the conservation area. Furthermore, the advertisement results in less than substantial harm to the significance of the grade II listed building, Church of St Luke and the locally listed building, Latimer Health Centre that is not judged to be outweighed by pubic benefit, contrary to policies LP1, LP3, LP4 and LP7 of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020), policies D3 and HC1 of The London Plan (2021) and Hackney&#x27;s Shopfront Design Guide.&lt;/p&gt;"
